   "shirt": "#2f6b5a",
   "glasses": false,
   "extra": "scarf"
  },
  "script": "Last winter I hiked to Dyatlov Pass in the northern Urals. In February 1959, nine experienced hikers cut their way out of their own tent and went out into minus thirty, half dressed. For sixty years people blamed aliens, the army, even a yeti. Standing on that slope, you understand the other answer. In 2021, scientists showed how a small slab of snow could break loose above a tent. Small enough to leave few traces. Big enough to make you run. It still gives me chills."
 },
